        "title": "What Living Things Need",
        "reading": "Every living thing on Earth needs the same basic things to stay alive. Plants and animals both need food, water, air, and shelter, though they get them in different ways. A plant makes its own food using sunlight, but it still needs water from the soil and air around its leaves. An animal must find or catch its food, drink water, and breathe air. Shelter keeps living things safe. A rabbit hides in a burrow, a bird builds a nest, and a plant's roots hold it steady in the soil. Living things also need space to grow. If a garden is too crowded, the plants cannot get enough light and water. When all its needs are met, a living thing can grow strong and even make babies, continuing the circle of life. Scientists test needs by taking one away at a time. Cover a plant so it gets no light, and it turns pale and weak. Give a pet no water, and it cannot survive long. These tests prove that every need matters.",
