        "reading": "A plant is like a small factory, and each part has a job. Roots grow underground and drink up water and nutrients from the soil. They also hold the plant steady, like an anchor. The stem is the plant's highway and backbone. It carries water up from the roots and food down from the leaves, and it holds the plant upright toward the sun. Leaves are the kitchens. They catch sunlight and use it to make food for the whole plant. Flowers have a special job: they attract bees and other insects that carry pollen, which helps the plant make seeds. Every part depends on the others. If the roots cannot find water, the leaves cannot make food, and the whole plant suffers. Some plants break the usual rules. Cactus spines are really leaves that save water. A Venus flytrap's leaves snap shut on insects. Still, every plant follows the same plan: roots drink, stems carry, leaves cook, and flowers make seeds. Learn the plan and you can understand any plant you meet.",
