        "reading": "Plants need different care at different stages of life. A seed needs water and warmth to wake up, but it does not need light yet because it lives off its packed food. A seedling needs gentle light and steady water as it builds its first leaves. A growing plant needs lots of sunlight to make food, plus water and nutrients from the soil. A flowering plant needs pollinators like bees, so gardeners plant bright blooms nearby. When fruits form, the plant needs extra water to fill them out. Farmers and gardeners who know these stages give each plant exactly what it needs, exactly when it needs it. That is how small seeds become huge harvests. Farmers use growth stages to plan harvests. They plant fast crops like lettuce for quick picking and slow crops like pumpkins for fall. Knowing each stage helps them water and feed plants at just the right time. A good farmer reads a field the way you read a story, stage by stage.",
