        "title": "Producers, Consumers, Decomposers",
        "reading": "Every ecosystem has three teams of living things. Producers make their own food using sunlight. Grass, trees, and algae are producers. Consumers eat other living things. A rabbit eats grass, a fox eats the rabbit, and you are a consumer when you eat lunch. Decomposers are nature's cleanup crew. Mushrooms, mold, and bacteria break down dead plants and animals, returning nutrients to the soil. Without decomposers, dead leaves would pile up forever and plants would run out of food. The three teams form a circle: producers feed consumers, decomposers recycle everything, and the nutrients grow new producers. Every bite you take connects you to all three teams. Humans are the ultimate consumers. We eat producers like wheat and consumers like chicken. We even use decomposers: yeast and bacteria make bread, cheese, and yogurt. Without the three teams, there would be no farms, no food, and no us. Every meal thanks all three.",
