        "title": "Life in a Pond",
        "reading": "A pond is a small world packed with life. Algae and water plants are the producers, making food from sunlight. Tiny creatures like water fleas eat the algae. Tadpoles munch on plants, and small fish eat the water fleas. Bigger fish, frogs, and turtles hunt the smaller animals. Herons stalk the edges, spearing fish with sharp beaks. Under the mud, decomposers like bacteria break down dead leaves and recycle nutrients. Dragonflies zip above the surface, laying eggs that hatch into underwater hunters. Every part connects. If fertilizer runs into the pond, algae grow wild, use up the oxygen, and fish can die, showing how delicate the balance is. Ponds change with the seasons. In spring, frogs lay eggs and tadpoles swarm. Summer brings dragonflies and blooming lilies. Fall slows everything as cold creeps in. In winter, life sleeps under ice, waiting. A pond is four ecosystems in one, turning with the year.",
