        "title": "Crispus Attucks and the Boston Massacre",
        "reading": "On a cold March night in 1770, angry colonists gathered around British soldiers in Boston. The crowd shouted, threw snowballs and sticks, and dared the soldiers to fire. In the confusion, the soldiers shot into the crowd, killing five colonists. The first to fall was Crispus Attucks, a Black sailor of African and Native ancestry who had escaped slavery years before. He had worked on whaling ships and was in Boston between voyages. Patriots called the event the Boston Massacre and used it to stir anger against Britain. Attucks became a symbol of the fight for liberty, honored as the first to die for American freedom. Attucks is honored with monuments in Boston today. His name appears on the memorial to the massacre's victims. For a man who escaped slavery to die for liberty, the honor is fitting. He wanted freedom and found it in history's memory. He ran from slavery toward freedom and found immortality in the cause of liberty.",
