        "title": "Mixtures and Solutions",
        "reading": "A mixture is two or more materials stirred together but not chemically joined. Trail mix is a mixture: you can still see the nuts and raisins. A solution is a special mixture where one material dissolves completely into another, like sugar in tea. You cannot see the sugar anymore, but it is still there. In a solution, the dissolved material is the solute and the liquid is the solvent. Air is a solution of gases. Every breath mixes oxygen into your lungs, and every sweet drink is a solution you can taste but not see. Solutions have limits: only so much sugar dissolves in tea. Past that point, it is saturated, and extra sugar sinks. Heat raises the limit, which is why hot tea sweetens easier. Every solution has its breaking point. Stir sugar into iced tea and watch the extra sink: you have found the saturation point. Even sweetness has limits.",
