        "title": "Kinetic and Potential Energy",
        "reading": "Energy is the ability to do work, and it comes in two main forms. Kinetic energy is the energy of motion: a rolling ball, a running child, a flowing river. The faster something moves, the more kinetic energy it has. Potential energy is stored energy waiting to happen: a ball held high, a stretched rubber band, water behind a dam. When the ball drops, potential becomes kinetic. Energy never disappears; it just changes form. A roller coaster trades potential for kinetic all the way down the track. Energy is never created or destroyed, only changed. This law rules everything from car engines to stars. Every joule is borrowed and returned. The universe runs on recycled energy. Energy is never created or destroyed, only changed from form to form. This single law rules car engines, roller coasters, and stars alike. The universe runs entirely on recycled energy. Not one joule is ever lost, only transformed.",
